StagefrightMetadataRetriever::parseMetaData() used sprintf with %f to format a float into a 32-byte buffer. An attacker-supplied float (e.g., FLT_MAX) could result in an output of up to 47 bytes, causing a stack buffer overflow.

This change replaces sprintf with snprintf in StagefrightMetadataRetriever.

Bug: 503551664
Test: manual repro with PoC
Flag: EXEMPT BUGFIX

Note: This was autogenerated by MendIt (go/androidmendit)
Cherrypick-From: https://googleplex-android-review.googlesource.com/q/commit:8407b6db81e0ba453f9aaeea9557a6596c6077a1
